WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.461
Build the pipeline. Keep the conversation.

00:00:03.994 --> 00:00:07.283
This is Duckpad: a visual workspace for

00:00:07.372 --> 00:00:09.417
turning data into answers.

00:00:09.861 --> 00:00:12.706
Drag in a step, connect your sources, and

00:00:12.883 --> 00:00:16.172
shape your data with simple controls or SQL.

00:00:16.706 --> 00:00:17.417
Need a hand?

00:00:17.861 --> 00:00:20.350
Ask the AI assistant about your flow.

00:00:20.794 --> 00:00:23.906
It reads your project, explains the logic,

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:26.217
and can make changes you can review and

00:00:26.306 --> 00:00:26.928
undo.

00:00:27.461 --> 00:00:30.039
Keep quality checks beside your SQL.

00:00:30.483 --> 00:00:33.683
Run data tests, inspect failing rows, and

00:00:33.772 --> 00:00:36.083
surface useful messages right where you

00:00:36.261 --> 00:00:36.528
work.

00:00:36.972 --> 00:00:39.817
Explore the result, then trace a value back

00:00:39.861 --> 00:00:41.150
to the data behind it.

00:00:41.683 --> 00:00:44.528
Every change is versioned with Git, so you

00:00:44.617 --> 00:00:47.372
can compare, branch, and keep moving.

00:00:47.817 --> 00:00:50.306
From a first connection to a result you

00:00:50.394 --> 00:00:51.372
understand.

00:00:51.817 --> 00:00:55.550
Duckpad. Build visually. Go deeper.
